<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Cadence — Portfolio</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    body {
      font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
      background-color: #F7F5F2;
      color: #141B21;
    }

    .hero {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 120px 24px 80px 24px;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 40px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .hero p.context {
      font-size: 18px;
      color: #2E3A46;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    .hero p.proof {
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #2E3A46;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .hero a.cta {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #A3501F;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    /* --- AI Recommendation Review --- */

    .recommendation {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 80px 24px;
    }

    .rec-card {
      background-color: #FFFFFF;
      border: 1px solid #2E3A46;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 40px;
    }

    .rec-card h2 {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 26px;
      line-height: 1.4;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .rec-why-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #2E3A46;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .rec-why-list {
      list-style: none;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .rec-why-list li {
      color: #A3501F;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: 16px;
      position: relative;
    }

    .rec-why-list li::before {
      content: "•";
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
    }

    .rec-worth {
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #141B21;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .rec-actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .rec-actions a {
      flex: 1;
      min-width: 120px;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 14px 20px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 15px;
      text-decoration: none;
      border: 1px solid #2E3A46;
      color: #2E3A46;
    }

    .rec-actions a.why-link {
      border-color: #C4622D;
      color: #A3501F;
    }

    /* --- Reasoning Artifact --- */

    .reasoning {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 80px 24px 120px 24px;
    }

    .reasoning h2 {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 32px;
      margin-bottom: 48px;
    }

    .r-block {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .r-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #2E3A46;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .r-block p {
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #2E3A46;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .r-hidden {
      margin: 56px 0;
      padding: 40px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid #2E3A46;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #2E3A46;
    }

    .r-hidden .r-label {
      color: #A3501F;
    }

    .r-hidden p {
      font-size: 22px;
      color: #141B21;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
/* --- Outcome States --- */

    .outcomes {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 24px 120px 24px;
    }

    .outcomes h2 {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 24px;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .outcome-row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 16px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .outcome-card {
      flex: 1;
      min-width: 180px;
      background-color: #FFFFFF;
      border: 1px solid #2E3A46;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .outcome-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #2E3A46;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .outcome-card p {
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #141B21;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
  </style>
</head>
    <section class="outcomes">
    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <div class="outcome-row">
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="outcome-label">Updated</div>
        <p>Confirmed. Your schedule now reflects the change.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="outcome-label">Modified</div>
        <p>Confirmed. Your adjustment has been saved.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="outcome-label">Original</div>
        <p>Nothing changed. Your schedule stays as it was.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
<body>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>When an AI changes your calendar, it should have to explain itself first — that's how it earns your trust.</h1>
    <p class="context">Cadence is a cycle-aware AI scheduling assistant — meet Aya, the assistant behind it.</p>
    <p class="proof">A CV can say you've "designed AI features." It can't show the actual decision of what reasoning to surface, and what to hide, when an algorithm changes someone's calendar without asking first — this case study can.</p>
    <a href="#recommendation" class="cta">See the moment this gets tested →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="recommendation" id="recommendation">
    <div class="rec-card">
      <h2>Move "Website Redesign" from Monday to Wednesday</h2>

      <div class="rec-why-label">Why</div>
      <ul class="rec-why-list">
        <li>Predicted creative score increases from 58% to 89%</li>
        <li>Sleep recovery is expected to improve</li>
        <li>No conflicting meetings</li>
        <li>Similar tasks have historically been completed 24% faster on comparable days</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rec-worth">Estimated time saved: 45 minutes</div>

      <div class="rec-actions">
        <a href="#">Approve</a>
        <a href="#">Edit</a>
        <a href="#">Decline</a>
        <a href="#reasoning" class="why-link">Why this recommendation? →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reasoning" id="reasoning">
    <h2>Why this recommendation?</h2>

    <div class="r-block">
      <div class="r-label">AI inputs received</div>
      <p>Cycle data, calendar availability, workload signals, and sleep/recovery trends.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="r-block">
      <div class="r-label">Information surfaced</div>
      <p>What made the recommendation screen — the creative-score shift, sleep impact, calendar conflicts, and historical task speed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="r-hidden">
      <div class="r-label">Information hidden</div>
      <p>Raw symptom logs, hormonal trend charts, and day-by-day mood scores didn't make the recommendation screen. They inform the model, but showing them here would turn a scheduling decision into a health dashboard — and bury the one thing you actually need to decide on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="r-block">
      <div class="r-label">Design rationale</div>
      <p>This is the right amount of transparency: enough reasoning to trust the recommendation, not so much that you have to interpret your own biometrics to use your calendar.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</body>
</html>
